 the unique maximizer of t(T, W)\namong regular tournamentons W.\ntournamenton is the unique maximizer of t(T, W) among regular tournamentons\nW; three 6-vertex tournaments T with this property are depicted in Figure 9.\nWe do not have a conjectured list of all such tournaments T and we leave their\ncharacterization as an open problem.\nProblem 4. Characterize which tournaments T satisfy that the constant tour-\nnamenton is the unique maximizer of t(T, W) among regular tournamentons W.\nNote that a resolution of Problem 4 together with Corollary 11 would yield a\nfull solution of [40, Problem 6.1] and Proposition 12 asserts that it is enough to\ninvestigate tournaments T with at most nine vertices.\nReferences\n[1] N. Behague, N. Morrison and J. A. Noel: Off-diagonal commonality of graphs\nvia entropy, SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics 38 (2024), 2335–2360.\n[2] G. R. Blakley and P. Roy: A H¨older type inequality for symmetric matrices\nwith nonnegative entries, Proceedings of the American Mathematical Society\n16 (1965), 1244–1245.\n[3] M. Buci´c, E. Long, A. Shapira and B. Sudakov: Tournament quasirandom-\nness from local counting, Combinatorica 41 (2021), 175–208.\n[4] T. Chan, D. Kr´al’, J. A. Noel, Y. Pehova, M. Sharifzadeh and J. Volec:\nCharacterization of quasirandom permutations by a pattern sum, Random\nStructures & Algorithms 57 (2020), 920–939.\n[5] T.-W. Chao, A. C. Antonir, A. Li and H.-H. H. Yu: Edge inducibility via\nlocal directed graphs, preprint arXiv:2509.24064 (2025).\n[6] T.-W. Chao and H.-H. H. Yu: Kruskal–Katona-type problems via the entropy\nmethod, Journal of Combinatorial Theory, Series B 169 (2024), 480–506.\n24--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(ibge012010_relat\\363rio_RECENSEADOR_SP.xls) (https://estaticog1.globo.com/2010/07/ibge/ibge012010_relatorio_RECENSEADOR_SP.pdf)\nciteturn2search13 [wordlim: 200] ROBSON PATRICIO DO NASCIMENTO — 2506.00878-5 — ITAQUAQUECETUBA — 67,5 — 253\nROBS